        "original_id": "d625dfa8-1cbe-5b49-bf5a-f880b080d820",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peggy Schuyler, Stephen Van Rensselaer III, Angelica Schuyler Church, Philip Jeremiah Schuyler, Elizabeth Schuyler Hamilton, John Barker Church, Alexander Hamilton\n- Organizations: the first private orphanage in New York City\n- Roles: wife, sister, sister-in-law, co-founder, deputy director\n\nFacts:\n- Elizabeth Schuyler Hamilton was born on August 9, 1757, and was sometimes called Eliza or Betsey.\n- Peggy Schuyler was the wife of Stephen Van Rensselaer III.\n- Peggy Schuyler was the sister of Angelica Schuyler Church, Philip Jeremiah Schuyler, and Elizabeth Schuyler Hamilton.\n- Peggy Schuyler was the sister-in-law of John Barker Church and Alexander Hamilton.\n- Elizabeth Schuyler Hamilton was a co-founder and deputy director of the first private orphanage in New York City.\n- Elizabeth Schuyler Hamilton died on November 9, 1854.",
